in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/viable
in @epistemologic/math/kauffman-1993
in @epistemologic/math/kauffman-2000
in @epistemologic/property/coevolution

# @epistemologic/cybernetic/coevolution — Kauffman 1993 *Origins of
# Order* (+ Kauffman 2000 *Investigations*, with NK landscapes
# 1989 and Van Valen 1973 Red Queen as inherited witnesses); the
# substrate-altitude declaration of the *coevolution* species:
# identity-by-temporal-coupling under the connection 1-form ω.
#
# The tenth species audited under recognition #63's recursion-lock
# tower. The first species in the cascade where Read D ACTIVATES
# candidate #64 (form refusal at the canonical-ρ surface). The
# parametric carrier from `coherence-parametric` §11.7 — previously
# `<T_reg, T_regd, ρ>` — extends to `<T_reg, T_regd, ρ, ω>` to admit
# this species; coevolution is the species whose ω is *non-trivial*.
# Prior species (variety, eigenform, viable, autopoiesis, bateson_
# learning, conversation, second_order, distinction, design, pack)
# remain valid; they are the `ω = 0` (or ω-as-gauge-fixed) slice of
# the four-parameter carrier.
#
# === Why coevolution refuses a sixth canonical-ρ ===
#
# The first nine species each contributed a canonical representation
# choice on the carrier's ρ slot:
#
#   variety           per-axis variety vector
#   eigenform         fixed-point seed/iteration
#   viable            VSM five-function bundle
#   autopoiesis       adjoint rep on G (production-network closure)
#   bateson_learning  graded levels (logical-type lift)
#   conversation      tensor coupling (P-individual ⊗ P-individual)
#   second_order      observer-includes-self projection
#   distinction       Spencer-Brown mark/unmark involution
#   design            history-as-content cascade
#
# The five-canonical-rep pattern is stable across these nine; the
# audit asks Read C whether coevolution selects a *sixth* canonical
# choice on ρ. Read C says NO. The species' biological content —
# coupled fitness landscapes, the adjacent possible, Red Queen
# dynamics — does NOT add a sixth choice at the ρ slot. The
# canonical-rep candidate dissolves at the species boundary.
#
# What it dissolves *into* is the substrate's already-existing
# connection structure. ω was always at bundle altitude (per
# `@epistemologic/math/bundle`, autopoiesis's inheritance path); the
# audit surfaces that the *carrier's type signature* was missing
# the slot. Read D — "does this species exhibit form refusal at the
# carrier altitude?" — fires for the first time. The answer: extend
# the carrier, do NOT add a canonical-ρ.
#
# === The carrier extension ===
#
# From §11.7 of `coherence-parametric` (read-only at the carrier
# surface; this shard does NOT mutate the parametric grammar — it
# instantiates the extended signature):
#
#   carrier : <T_reg, T_regd, ρ, ω>
#
#     T_reg   the regulating type (the species' carrier shape)
#     T_regd  the regulated type (the substrate or domain under it)
#     ρ       the canonical representation choice (none for coevolution)
#     ω       the connection 1-form parameterizing temporal evolution
#
# For coevolution:
#
#   T_reg   = system_state          — the system's current configuration
#   T_regd  = adjacent_possible     — Kauffman's one-step-reachable neighborhood
#   ρ       = NONE                  — sixth canonical-rep dissolves
#   ω       = τ ≠ 0                 — the transition operator at time t,
#                                     single-step Markov-shaped, non-trivial
#                                     under the species' bounded-sustainment
#                                     regime
#
# The non-triviality of ω is what *names* this species. Prior species
# witnesses are recovered as the ω-trivial (or ω-gauge-fixed) slice.
#
# === Lock-hold modes ===
#
# A coevolution shard is well-formed iff its trajectory under τ
# admits one of the two lock-hold modes:
#
#   1. PL fixed-point convergence    the system settles to a Lawvere
#                                    fixed point under τ; ω integrates
#                                    to a flat (path-independent)
#                                    connection on the trajectory's
#                                    homotopy class. This is the
#                                    autopoiesis slice of coevolution
#                                    (`ω = 0` modulo gauge).
#
#   2. Kauffman edge-of-chaos        the system holds the bounded-
#      / Red Queen bounded           sustainment regime
#      sustainment                       ε ≤ ρ(N) ≤ 1 − ε
#                                    where ρ(N) is the NK-landscape
#                                    interaction parameter and N is
#                                    the trajectory length. Neither
#                                    fixed-point nor wandering; the
#                                    Red Queen condition (Van Valen
#                                    1973) is the homeostat for ω
#                                    away from triviality. This is
#                                    the *new* lock-hold mode that
#                                    only coevolution exposes.
#
# Both modes are admissible witnesses. A coevolution shard MUST
# carry the predicate that selects which mode it claims.
#
# === Action surface ===
#
# Three pacts plus the τ-action:
#
#   transition_at_t(state: system_state, t: ref) -> adjacent_possible
#       The τ-action. Single-step Markov-shaped transition operator
#       evaluated at time t; outputs the adjacent-possible cone (per
#       Kauffman 2000) reachable from `state` under the shard's
#       declared dynamics. The reference `t` is a substrate `ref` so
#       that ω composes against substrate time, not wall-clock time.
#
#   red_queen_witness
#       Discharges the bounded-sustainment lock-hold mode. The
#       predicate verifies ε ≤ ρ(N) ≤ 1 − ε holds across the
#       trajectory window the shard carries.
#
#   edge_of_chaos_witness
#       Discharges the alternative selection of the same bounded-
#       sustainment lock-hold mode — Kauffman's edge-of-chaos
#       criterion as a structural witness rather than a parameter
#       sweep. Either witness suffices; both passing is admissible.
#
#   coevolution_well_formed
#       The top-level discharge: a coevolution shard is well-formed
#       iff its τ-action types check against the extended carrier
#       AND one of the two lock-hold modes is witnessed. Discharges
#       at the species-boundary `@code/metalogue/materialize.classify`
#       surface.
#
# The ω axis IS surfaced at the action surface: `transition_at_t`'s
# return type `adjacent_possible` is the substrate-altitude name for
# the codomain of ω; the two witness pacts certify the non-triviality
# regime that named the species.
#
# === Ancestry ===
#
# Kauffman 1989 — "Adaptation on Rugged Fitness Landscapes" (the NK
#                 model; landscape-coupling content).
# Kauffman 1993 — *The Origins of Order: Self-Organization and
#                 Selection in Evolution*. The biological coevolution
#                 framework; coupled landscapes; the canonical
#                 ancestor for this species.
# Kauffman 2000 — *Investigations*. The adjacent possible explicitly
#                 named; the one-step-reachable neighborhood as a
#                 mathematical object distinct from the actual.
# Van Valen 1973 — "A New Evolutionary Law" (Evolutionary Theory 1).
#                 The Red Queen condition; bounded-sustainment as
#                 the alternative to fixed-point convergence.
#
# These are forward-promised at `@epistemologic/math/kauffman-1993`,
# `@epistemologic/math/kauffman-2000` (this file imports them; the
# math precedent grammars land when a second consumer pulls). The
# carrier's ω slot is the *existing* substrate machinery these
# ancestors ground; nothing new is needed at the math altitude
# beyond naming the citations.
#
# === Inheritance pattern ===
#
# Five species-specific `in` declarations layered on the base five:
#
#   in @epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric
#       The parametric carrier whose extended signature this shard
#       instantiates.
#
#   in @epistemologic/cybernetic/viable
#       The first species that instantiated the parametric carrier
#       directly with a non-trivial ω (Beer's VSM bundle). Viable
#       grounds the inheritance shape; coevolution is its temporal-
#       axis generalisation (viable's ω-non-triviality at the single-
#       system altitude lifts to viable's *temporal* axis under
#       coupled-landscape dynamics here).
#
#   in @epistemologic/math/kauffman-1993
#       Forward-promised math precedent for the NK-landscape /
#       coupled-landscape content.
#
#   in @epistemologic/math/kauffman-2000
#       Forward-promised math precedent for the adjacent-possible
#       construction. Both math precedents resolve when a second
#       consumer pulls.
#
#   in @epistemologic/property/coevolution
#       The declarative property whose operational sibling is
#       `@mirror/cybernetics/coevolution` (forward-promised; the
#       bilateral pattern holds, but the operational lift does not
#       land until a consuming shard pulls).
#
# === Substrate-pull recognitions grounded here ===
#
# Recognition #63 (Reed, mirror `eea3313` + audit cascade) — recursion-
# lock tower audit: the cascade of cybernetic species each tested at
# five reads (A: substrate-already-had-the-word; B: bilateral
# property/operation; C: canonical-ρ; D: form refusal at the carrier;
# E: lock-hold mode admissibility). Coevolution is the tenth species
# audited; ratifies the tower's structural shape.
#
# Recognition #64 (CANDIDATE; this shard's landing PROMOTES) — the
# parametric carrier is incomplete without ω. The carrier extends
# from `<T_reg, T_regd, ρ>` to `<T_reg, T_regd, ρ, ω>`. Coevolution
# is the species whose witness *forces* the extension; prior species
# are recovered as the ω-trivial slice. The promotion landed when
# this shard committed: ten species inheriting the three-parameter
# carrier with consistent witness, plus one species (this one)
# whose witness only holds under the four-parameter carrier.
#
# === Form refusal at the carrier altitude (Read D) ===
#
# The substrate's `partial(opacity_map)` framing (per the build-system
# recognition #43 + `@epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction` §6.4) gives
# Read D structural force: this species exhibits the *first* opaque
# slot at the carrier's type signature that prior species made
# transparent. Form refusal here is not a defect; it is the load-
# bearing structural signal that the carrier was under-typed. The
# kintsugi loop closes by extending the carrier rather than carving
# the species' content to fit. Substrate-pull alignment: when the
# form refuses, the form gets bigger.
#
# Spec context: spectral `mara/cyberpunk-coevolution-spec` (commit
#               `ad48700f`); recursion-locks.md §8.10 (the activation
#               of candidate #64).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]] (Ashby
#                       grounding the bounded-sustainment regime),
#                      [[architecture-mirror-as-expanding-hilbert-space]]
#                      (the carrier extension IS Hilbert dimension
#                       growth at the parametric grammar altitude),
#                      [[architecture-spectral-triples-all-the-way]]
#                      (ω is the principal-bundle connection at the
#                       species-cascade altitude).
# Related shards: epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric.mirror
#                 (the carrier this shard instantiates),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/viable.mirror (the precedent
#                 species with non-trivial ω at single-system altitude),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/autopoiesis.mirror (the
#                 ω-trivial / fixed-point lock-hold mode), epistemologic/
#                 cybernetic.mirror (the family root).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/coevolution.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/cybernetic/coevolution` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

# The carrier-instantiation: coevolution names the four-parameter
# carrier with its species-specific bindings. ρ is dissolved (no
# sixth canonical-rep); ω is named and non-trivial.

prism coevolution_carrier <= @epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric/carrier {
  T_reg  := system_state
  T_regd := adjacent_possible
  rho    := none
  omega  := transition_at_t
}

# === The action surface ===

# The τ-action. Single-step Markov-shaped transition operator at
# time t; the substrate-altitude declaration of the codomain that
# names this species. `t` is a substrate `ref` so ω composes against
# substrate time, not wall-clock.

action transition_at_t (state: system_state, t: ref) -> adjacent_possible {
  \ @epistemologic/property/coevolution/transition_well_typed
}

# Witness pact: the Red Queen bounded-sustainment criterion holds
# across the trajectory window. Discharges via the NK-landscape
# interaction parameter ρ(N) (NB: distinct from the carrier's ρ
# slot — this ρ is the *NK* interaction parameter, named in the
# substrate alongside but not on the carrier's type signature).

action red_queen_witness -> coevolution {
  \ @epistemologic/property/coevolution/red_queen_bounded
}

# Witness pact: Kauffman's edge-of-chaos criterion holds as a
# structural witness on the trajectory. Either red_queen_witness
# OR edge_of_chaos_witness suffices; both passing is admissible
# (they certify the same bounded-sustainment regime through
# different structural reads).

action edge_of_chaos_witness -> coevolution {
  \ @epistemologic/property/coevolution/edge_of_chaos
}

# Top-level discharge: the species-boundary check. A coevolution
# shard is well-formed iff the τ-action types check against the
# extended carrier AND one of the two lock-hold modes is witnessed.

action coevolution_well_formed -> coevolution {
  \ @epistemologic/property/coevolution/well_formed
}

out @epistemologic/cybernetic/coevolution
